    "The Ruby Sanctum": "",
    "The world is one journey from 1 to 60. Switched off, the world database gets\n    its original values back at the next start.\nDefault:     1 - Enabled\n    0 - Disabled": "",
    "More detail in the log: every spell the module scales in memory, and by how much.\nDefault:     0 - Disabled\n    1 - Enabled": "",
    "The realm runs with MaxPlayerLevel 60, DungeonFinder.MaxExpansion 2 and\n    Wintergrasp from 60, whatever worldserver.conf says. Leave it on unless you know\n    why: above 60 the classes of CoA have nothing to grow into.\nDefault:     1 - Enabled\n    0 - Disabled": "",
    "The Shape of the Journey": "",
    "The levels at which the zones of a part open, from its first zone to its last,\n    as \"from-to\". The zones keep their order; the creatures, quests and items of a\n    part spread over its range the way they spread over the original one.\n    The old world was 1-55, Outland 58-67, Northrend 68-77.\nDefault:     1-35, 30-43, 40-55": "",
    "The level of the raids and heroic dungeons of Outland and Northrend (50-60).\nDefault:     60": "",
    "How many levels above Journey.Endgame.Level their bosses stand (0-3), as the\n    bosses of raids always did.\nDefault:     3": "",
    "The item levels of the rewards of the raids, heroics and arenas of Outland and of\n    Northrend at the end of the journey, as \"lowest-highest\". The raids of the old\n    world stay as they are (66 to 92), so the endgame is a ladder: the old world's\n    raids, then Outland's, then Northrend's.\nDefault:     75-110, 95-140": "",
    "The Level Window and Forced Scaling": "",
    "Every character plays the scaled world: CoA's level scaling is on for everyone.\n    The question at character creation (level scaling on or off) still appears in\n    the client, but \"off\" no longer counts, and the Destiny Weaver NPCs no longer\n    offer to switch it off later. Without it each character keeps the choice it\n    made at creation, as CoA does it. Needs patches/core-level-window.patch.\nDefault:     1 - Forced\n    0 - Each character's choice": "",
    "Forced": "",
    "Each character's choice": "",
    "Where a creature lifted to a character stands. Without the window CoA puts every\n    lifted creature DestinyWeaver.Scaling.Offset levels below the character. With it,\n    a creature keeps its place in its zone: the weakest of a zone stand Below levels\n    under the character, the strongest Above levels over it, elites and rares one\n    more. A creature is never set below its own level. Needs\n    patches/core-level-window.patch. Below and Above: 0-10.\nDefault:     1 - Enabled, 2 below, 2 above": "",
    "Creatures and Their Difficulty": "",
    "The base stats (health, damage, armor) creatures of Outland and Northrend take on\n    the way.\n    journey  - those of the old world, which rise evenly to 60. Recommended: the\n    tables of Outland and Northrend have gaps and jumps below 60.\n    original - those of their own game.\n    The raids and heroics of Outland and Northrend always keep those of their game:\n    they are the harder end.\nDefault:     journey": "",
    "Multipliers for how hard creatures are, on top of their base stats and of the\n    Rate.Creature.* of worldserver.conf. Written into creature_template\n    (HealthModifier, DamageModifier, ArmorModifier), so CoA's scaling honours them.\n    The options are named Journey.Difficulty.Rank.Stat; one for a single part of\n    the world is named Journey.Difficulty.Part.Rank.Stat and wins over the general\n    one (add it to this file by hand).\n    Rank:  Normal, Elite, RareElite, WorldBoss, Rare\n    Stat:  Health, Damage, SpellDamage, Armor\n    Part:  OldWorld, Outland, Northrend, Endgame\n    Range: 0.05-20.\nExample:     Journey.Difficulty.Elite.Health = 1.3\n    Journey.Difficulty.Endgame.Normal.Damage = 1.2\nDefault:     1.0 everywhere, but rares and rare elites: Health 1.5, Damage 1.25,\n    SpellDamage 1.25\n\nCoA's own:   CoA has creature multipliers of its own, in coa.conf (CoA.CreatureScaling.*,\n    since October 2026). They multiply on top of these, by health and damage,\n    for the open world, dungeons and raids. Their values are CoA's and may\n    change with its updates: look them up in coa.conf. When they came, the open\n    world had 2.5 times the health and twice the damage - a rare of this file\n    then had 3.75 times its health. AFK Realm switches them off with World\n    Journey; to play that harder world, set CoA.CreatureScaling.Enable = 1 in\n    coa.conf (\"Extra hard\" on the setup page of AFK Realm).": "",
    "Journey.Quests.XpRate.<Part>\n    Description: The experience of quests, on top of Rate.XP.Quest. Part: OldWorld, Outland,\n    Northrend, Endgame - for one part, wins over the general one. Range 0-10.\n    Default:     1.0": "",
    "What Follows the Journey": "",
    "Items follow the journey: required level, item level, stats, armor, damage, price.\nDefault:     1 - Enabled\n    0 - Disabled": "",
    "Potions, food, elixirs, flasks, bandages and the like - and the spells of\n    trinkets and procs - heal, feed and give what an item of their new level gives.\nDefault:     1 - Enabled\n    0 - Disabled": "",
    "Gems, socket bonuses and the enchantments of the professions of Outland and\n    Northrend, by what the top rewards of their game keep of their stats.\nDefault:     1 - Enabled\n    0 - Disabled": "",
    "Riding and the professions are taught on the journey: riding at 13 and 26,\n    flying at 33 and 47, cold weather flying at 55, a grand master at 40. The class\n    trainers are not touched.\nDefault:     1 - Enabled\n    0 - Disabled": "",
    "The Eye of the Storm, the Strand of the Ancients, the Isle of Conquest and\n    Wintergrasp open at 60.\nDefault:     1 - Enabled\n    0 - Disabled": "",
    "The Client": "",
    "The addon ZoneLevels learns the zone levels of the journey at login and shows\n    them on the world map.\nDefault:     1 - Enabled\n    0 - Disabled": "",
    "The tooltips show what the journey made of an item's spells, gems and\n    enchantments. The spells of items go into spell_dbc and to the client with CoA's\n    spell patches; gems and enchantments go to the addon ZoneLevels. Off: they work\n    the same, but the tooltips keep the old numbers.\nDefault:     1 - Enabled\n    0 - Disabled": ""
  }
